/P 40 0 R
/T (     Strong Interest in Clean Energy Alternatives)
/E (     Strong Interest in Clean Energy Alternatives)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (Despite these challenges, there is a strong and encouraging interest in clean energy alternatives. A large proportion of respondents expressed willingness to adopt solutions such as solar power, while many others indicated openness to making the transition. This reflects a meaningful shift in mindset where clean energy is no longer seen as unfamiliar, but as a viable and desirable option.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 40 0 R
/T (     Access, Not Interest, Is the Barrier)
/E (     Access, Not Interest, Is the Barrier)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 40 0 R
/E (What becomes clear is that the barrier is not a lack of interest, but the difficulty of access. Upfront costs, limited financing options, and lack of flexible payment systems continue to stand in the way of adoption. Demand for clean energy is present and growing, but without deliberate efforts to address affordability and accessibility, this demand will remain largely unmet.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
